### - Secrets from files (Docker secrets, Kubernetes, Portainer)
## - Every SCANOPY_<NAME> below, on the server and the daemon, can be read from a file
## - instead: set SCANOPY_<NAME>_FILE to the file's path. Trailing newlines are trimmed.
## - Setting both SCANOPY_<NAME> and SCANOPY_<NAME>_FILE, or pointing _FILE at a file
## - that is missing or unreadable, stops startup with an error naming the variable.
## - The daemon's SCANOPY_LOG_FILE is a log path, not a secret file; its file form is
## - SCANOPY_LOG_FILE_FILE.
# SCANOPY_SMTP_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/smtp_password
# SCANOPY_DATABASE_URL_FILE=/run/secrets/database_url

### - Server
SCANOPY_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/scanopy
SCANOPY_PUBLIC_URL=http://your-domain.com:60072
SCANOPY_LOG_LEVEL=info
# SCANOPY_DISABLE_REGISTRATION=true
# SCANOPY_DISABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN=true
## - uncomment below when using HTTPS
# SCANOPY_USE_SECURE_SESSION_COOKIES=true

### - SMTP (optional - for password reset and notifications)
## - Every SMTP connection is encrypted; there is no plaintext mode and no setting to
## - turn encryption on. The PORT selects which kind: 465 (the default when
## - SCANOPY_SMTP_PORT is unset) is implicit TLS, and any other port uses STARTTLS,
## - which is what submission ports like 587 and 25 expect. STARTTLS is required, not
## - opportunistic: if the upgrade fails, the send is aborted rather than downgraded.
## - All four of RELAY, USERNAME, PASSWORD and EMAIL must be set or email stays off.
## - Set EMAIL to the same mailbox as USERNAME unless that account has been granted
## - permission to send as another address; most providers reject a mismatch.
# SCANOPY_SMTP_RELAY=smtp.gmail.com
# SCANOPY_SMTP_USERNAME=your-email@gmail.com
# SCANOPY_SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-password
# SCANOPY_SMTP_EMAIL=scanopy@yourdomain.com
# SCANOPY_SMTP_PORT=587
##
## - Microsoft 365 accepts submission ONLY on 587 with STARTTLS - it does not listen on
## - 465, so the default port fails to connect. Set the port explicitly:
# SCANOPY_SMTP_RELAY=smtp.office365.com
# SCANOPY_SMTP_PORT=587
# SCANOPY_SMTP_USERNAME=scanopy@yourdomain.com
# SCANOPY_SMTP_PASSWORD=your-password
# SCANOPY_SMTP_EMAIL=scanopy@yourdomain.com
## - 365 also requires tenant-side setup that Scanopy cannot do for you: SMTP AUTH must
## - be enabled for the mailbox (off by default for tenants created after January 2020),
## - security defaults must be off, and the account must not require MFA.
##
## - Amazon SES only: the region of the SES account. When set, the server logs an error at
## - startup if the SNS topic ARN or an email-smtp.<region>.amazonaws.com relay names a
## - different region. SES publishes feedback only to a topic in its own region.
# SCANOPY_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
##
## - Amazon SES only: the SNS topic that delivers bounce and complaint notifications.
## - Subscribe {PUBLIC_URL}/api/email/feedback/sns to it over HTTPS. A complaint turns off
## - every pausable email for that user.
# SCANOPY_EMAIL_FEEDBACK_SNS_TOPIC_ARN=arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:123456789012:ses-feedback
##
## - Amazon SES only: validate signup addresses with GetEmailAddressInsights ($0.01 per
## - signup) in SCANOPY_AWS_REGION. Signups with a LOW validity verdict, or a disposable or
## - random-looking address, are rejected; any SES error lets the signup through. The region
## - and both keys must be set or validation stays off. These are the keys of an IAM user
## - allowed only ses:GetEmailAddressInsights, not the SES SMTP credentials above.
# SCANOPY_EMAIL_VALIDATION_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIA...
# SCANOPY_EMAIL_VALIDATION_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret-access-key

### - Email logging (LOCAL TESTING ONLY - never set this in production)
## - Sends nothing. Logs every email at INFO and writes the rendered message
## - (.html + .txt) to this directory so it can be reviewed in a browser.
## - Takes precedence over SMTP: when set, no mail is delivered even
## - if credentials are configured.
## - The written files contain full email bodies IN PLAINTEXT, including
## - password-reset and verification tokens. Anyone who can read the directory
## - can take over an account.
# SCANOPY_EMAIL_LOG_DIR=/tmp/scanopy-emails

### - License key (optional)
## - Unlocks a self-hosted plan. Copy it from Settings > License in Scanopy Cloud.
## - The server reads it at startup, so run `docker compose up -d` after setting it.
## - `docker compose restart` does not pick up a changed .env.
# SCANOPY_LICENSE_KEY=

### - License check-ins (LOCAL TESTING ONLY)
## - An online license key fetches its entitlement from Scanopy Cloud
## - (https://app.scanopy.net). Point it at a local server to test check-ins
## - against a cloud instance you are running yourself.
# SCANOPY_LICENSE_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:60072

### - Release check (optional)
## - A self-hosted server asks GitHub for the latest Scanopy release at startup and
## - twice a day after, and shows admins a banner when an upgrade is out. The request
## - is an anonymous GET to api.github.com that sends no key, id or version.
## - Set this to stop the check.
# SCANOPY_DISABLE_UPDATE_CHECK=true

### - Download gateway (optional)
## - The daemon install and upgrade commands a licensed self-hosted server generates
## - download through get.scanopy.net and docker.scanopy.net, which count downloads
## - and fall back to GitHub. Set this to download from GitHub and ghcr.io directly.
# SCANOPY_DISABLE_DOWNLOAD_GATEWAY=true

### - To configure OIDC (optional), use the oidc.toml.example file

### - Private CA (optional)
## - PEM file with one or more CA certificates to trust in addition to the bundled
## - public roots. Use it when your OIDC issuer, SMTP relay, daemons or license server
## - present certificates signed by your own CA. The file is read once at startup; if it
## - is missing, unreadable or holds no certificates, the server refuses to start.
## - The daemon takes the same variable (or --trusted-ca-bundle) for its connections to
## - the server and to UniFi controllers.
# SCANOPY_TRUSTED_CA_BUNDLE=/etc/scanopy/ca-bundle.pem

### - Metrics (optional - for Prometheus/Grafana)
# SCANOPY_METRICS_TOKEN=your-secure-token-here
## - Restrict metrics access to specific IPs/CIDRs (comma-separated)
# SCANOPY_EXTERNAL_SERVICE_PROMETHEUS_ALLOWED_IPS=192.168.1.0/24,10.0.0.1

### - Daemon
# SCANOPY_DAEMON_API_KEY=<autogenerated>
